        "content": "<p>Let me show my ignorance. Is this OK?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RingTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Kaehler</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instCommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toCommSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toDistrib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMulZeroClass</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible_and_instances</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- works</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Tactic `rfl` failed: The left-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  CommRing.toCommSemiring.toNonAssocSemiring.toDistrib.toMul</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">is not definitionally equal to the right-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  TensorProduct.instSemiring.toNonAssocSemiring.toMulZeroClass.toMul</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">R S : Type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝⁴ : CommRing R</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝³ : CommRing S</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝² : Algebra R S</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">T : Type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝¹ : CommRing T</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">inst✝ : Algebra R T</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ CommRing.toCommSemiring.toNonAssocSemiring.toDistrib.toMul =</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    TensorProduct.instSemiring.toNonAssocSemiring.toMulZeroClass.toMul</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instCommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toCommSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toDistrib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMulZeroClass</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is two defeq but not reducibly defeq instances of <code>Mul (T ⊗[R] S)</code>. I don't really understand reducibility, and I think recent changes in 4.29 have made me understand it even less. If someone wants to explain why we care about <code>with_reducible</code> like I'm a beginner, that would be great.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>To un-xy, this is me trying to debug this <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/116290-rss/topic/Significant.20commits.20to.20mathlib4/near/584318088\">#rss &gt; Significant commits to mathlib4 @ 💬</a> . If the above code is OK and doesn't indicate a problem, then my real question is: why the heck is Lean taking a 6-figure amount of heartbeats to check that <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/kbuzzard/9c0bd1ba7facb3586d04d6d26fdfd0a3\">these two instances</a> are defeq (answer: because it is going on a very long unfolding adventure) when all universes match up and the instances are defeq with <code>with_reducible_and_instances</code>? Why doesn't it just go \"yup\"?</p>",
        "id": 584513366,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1775758214
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Since instances are compared in the <code>with_reducible_and_instances</code> transparency, it is not so relevant whether they unify in <code>with_reducible</code> transparency.</p>\n<p>Could you share a MWE of the slow unification you are talking about?</p>",
        "id": 584939689,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1775902810
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Algebra.Extension.tensorToH1Cotangent_bijective_of_flat#doc\">docs#Algebra.Extension.tensorToH1Cotangent_bijective_of_flat</a> is the proof I was looking at. The thing which is very wrong about it is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">async</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">12558738.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">addDecl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▼</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Kernel</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">12558626.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">typechecking</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">declarations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Extension</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tensorToH1Cotangent_bijective_of_flat</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but it is also taking a 7-figure number of heartbeats to elaborate and at least part of the reason this is happening is that the trace contains things like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">                        </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">287140.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instSMulOfMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which I'm very confused about; why is this taking so long when everything is the same at <code>reducible_and_instances</code>?</p>",
